    {
      "id": "ao4scgg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Composition of the Atmosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The atmosphere is primarily composed of Nitrogen (78%) and Oxygen (21%), along with trace gases like Argon (0.93%) and Carbon Dioxide (0.036%).",
        "Troposphere is the lowermost layer containing almost all water vapor and aerosols, where all weather phenomena take place.",
        "Stratosphere houses the vital Ozone Layer that protects the Earth from harmful solar ultraviolet rays.",
        "Mesosphere is the coldest layer of the atmosphere where temperature drops to -100°C and meteors burn up upon entry.",
        "Thermosphere includes the Ionosphere, which enables long-distance radio communication by reflecting radio waves back to Earth."
      ],
      "id": "oa9bkya"
    },
