    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "b9uufsd",
      "content": "• Third layer of the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mtscx45",
      "content": "• Meteors burn up due to friction in this layer."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "78bph4d",
      "content": "• It is the coldest layer."
    },
    {
      "id": "jbzlys1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Thermosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ti6qww7",
      "content": "• Temperature rises sharply with height."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hjn042k",
      "content": "• Contains ionized gases forming the ionosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5jojsed",
      "content": "• Important for radio communication."
    },
    {
      "id": "w0pb2yv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Exosphere"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gint67a",
      "content": "• Outermost layer of the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pjh3g7e",
      "content": "• Gradually merges into outer space."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Troposphere height varies from approximately 8 km at the poles to 18 km at the equator.",
        "The Normal Lapse Rate in the Troposphere is a temperature decrease of 6.5°C per 1,000 meters of altitude.",
        "Commercial jet aircraft usually fly in the lower Stratosphere to avoid weather disturbances.",
        "Ionosphere contains electrically charged ions that reflect radio waves back to Earth, making wireless communication possible."
      ],
      "id": "6gveohp"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dxegfvh",
      "content": "• Contains very thin air."
    },
    {
      "id": "4l6cu2z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xzz6nts",
      "content": "• Nitrogen is the most abundant gas in the atmosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "q4y034w",
      "content": "• Ozone layer is located in the stratosphere."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g6zo0qf",
      "content": "• Troposphere contains most weather phenomena."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hfmjk2c",
      "content": "• Mesosphere is the coldest layer."
    }
  ],
